# 31. TESTING REQUIREMENTS

Test these end-to-end flows:

Test A: New user registers, completes a profile, and reaches Home.

Test B: A rider creates a ride and sees it in the appropriate search results.

Test C: Another rider searches, opens the ride, and sends a join request.

Test D: The organiser accepts the request, and the rider sees the updated status.

Test E: Accepted participants can access the correct chat; unauthorised users cannot.

Test F: A user joins an open community and requests membership in a restricted community.

Test G: A community admin approves a membership request and creates an event.

Test H: A user RSVPs and sees the correct event status.

Test I: A user blocks another user, and server-side messaging restrictions work.

Test J: A user submits a report, and an authorised admin can review and resolve it.

Test K: Ride capacity cannot be exceeded, including simultaneous join requests.

Test L: A cancelled ride is removed from active results and participants receive an update.

Test M: Private profile information and precise location are not exposed publicly.

Test N: Network errors and retry attempts do not create duplicate records.

Add automated tests for important business rules where the environment supports them. Run the application, execute available tests, and fix errors.

